THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
SRC_001 changes the fixed point in violation of the problem's determinism guarantee: the post-hoc demotion of accepted nodes lacking a minimal defeat tree whose leaves are committed roots alters the least fixpoint computed in Pass 1, so the semantics is no longer the skeptical fixed point of spec §4. Because demotion removes accepted nodes, a previously reinstated node can lose its support and cascade into further demotions, meaning reinstatement is not merely a constructive by-product but requires a fresh stabilization that the traversal as described does not perform. Thus the committed-root-validity and determinism guarantees are not preserved.

TARGET:
Replace the single-pass skeptical fixpoint with a two-phase 'commit-then-explain' semantics: after the least fixpoint stabilizes, run a polynomial-time traversal that requires every accepted node to have at least one minimal defeat tree whose leaves are committed roots, and every refuted node to have a defeat tree explaining the defeat. Nodes failing the explanation check are demoted to suspended. This preserves determinism and polynomial cost because the traversal is on the already-computed labels, and it makes reinstatement a constructive by-product rather than an implicit label.